    text class complex(real=0, imag=0)
    text Convert a single string or number to a complex number, or create a complex number from real and imaginary parts.
    text Examples:
    text >>> complex('+1.23') (1.23+0j) >>> complex('-4.5j') -4.5j >>> complex('-1.23+4.5j') (-1.23+4.5j) >>> complex('\t( -1.23+4.5J )\n') (-1.23+4.5j) >>> complex('-Infinity+NaNj') (-inf+nanj) >>> complex(1.23) (1.23+0j) >>> complex(imag=-4.5) -4.5j >>> complex(-1.23, 4.5) (-1.23+4.5j)
    link float() #float
