    text enumerate()
    text start
    text iterable
    text >>> seasons = ['Spring', 'Summer', 'Fall', 'Winter'] >>> list(enumerate(seasons)) [(0, 'Spring'), (1, 'Summer'), (2, 'Fall'), (3, 'Winter')] >>> list(enumerate(seasons, start=1)) [(1, 'Spring'), (2, 'Summer'), (3, 'Fall'), (4, 'Winter')]
    text Equivalent to:
    text def enumerate(iterable, start=0): n = start for elem in iterable: yield n, elem n += 1
