      text locals
      text (
      text )
      link ¶ #locals
    text Return a mapping object representing the current local symbol table, with variable names as the keys, and their currently bound references as the values.
    link exec() #exec
    link eval() #eval
    link globals() #globals
    text At class scope, it returns the namespace that will be passed to the metaclass constructor.
    text When using exec() or eval() with separate local and global arguments, it returns the local namespace passed in to the function call.
    text In all of the above cases, each call to locals() in a given frame of execution will return the same mapping object. Changes made through the mapping object returned from locals() will be visible as assigned, reassigned, or deleted local variables, and assigning, reassigning, or deleting local variables will immediately affect the contents of the returned mapping object.
    link "optimized scope" ../glossary.html#term-optimized-scope
    text locals()
    text not
    text not
    text Calling locals() as part of a comprehension in a function, generator, or coroutine is equivalent to calling it in the containing scope, except that the comprehension’s initialised iteration variables will be included. In other scopes, it behaves as if the comprehension were running as a nested function.
    text Calling locals() as part of a generator expression is equivalent to calling it in a nested generator function.
    text Changed in version 3.12: danger
